  "result": "I fixed two bugs in `src/`, and `npm test` now passes all 243 tests. The tests themselves are unchanged.\n\n1. **Tax was charged before the discount** (`src/cart.js`). `total()` added tax to the subtotal first and then took off the discount, even though the code comment says discounts apply to the pre-tax amount. It now takes the discount off the subtotal first and adds tax to what's left. For example, $100 with a $20 discount and 10% tax now comes to $88 instead of $90. Percent discounts already gave the right totals, because the order doesn't matter when both steps are percentages. That's why only the fixed-discount test failed on this.\n2. **A fixed discount could make the total negative** (`src/discount.js`). If the discount was larger than the subtotal, the total went below zero ($5 with a $20 discount gave −14.5). The result is now floored at 0.",
